### What’s happening?

1. **`map.loadImage` no longer accepts a callback** –  
   Starting with **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** the method was changed to **return a `Promise`** instead of taking a `(err, image)` callback. Because the callback is ignored, the promise is never resolved and the image never gets added, so your custom marker icons disappear.

2. **Marker icons are missing** because the image you tried to load never made it into the style’s sprite (`map.addImage('pin', …)`). Once the image is added correctly, the markers will appear again.

---

## Fix it – two ways

### A. Modern, promise-based code (recommended)

```javascript
// Make sure the map is fully loaded before you call loadImage / addImage
map.once('load', async () => {
  try {
    // loadImage now returns a promise that resolves to { data: ImageBitmap }
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png');

    // addImage can be called directly; the second argument is the ImageBitmap
    map.addImage('pin', img);

    // Now you can use the image in a layer or a SymbolLayer
    map.addLayer({
      id: 'my-pins',
      type: 'symbol',
      source: 'my-geojson',
      layout: {
        'icon-image': 'pin',
        'icon-size': 0.8
      }
    });
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to load marker image:', err);
  }
});
```

**Key points**

| What changed? | How to write it now |
|---------------|---------------------|
| `map.loadImage(url, cb)` | `const { data } = await map.loadImage(url)` **or** `map.loadImage(url).then(({data}) => …)` |
| Returned value | An object `{ data: ImageBitmap }` (the image bitmap). |
| Error handling | Use `try / catch` (async/await) or `.catch(err => …)` on the promise. |
| Timing | Call after the map’s `load` event (or after any style change that could reset the sprite). |

### B. Back-compatible shim (if you must keep the old callback style)

If you are still on a MapLibre version **< 4.0.0** (unlikely if you installed the latest) you can keep the callback, but for the *latest* version you can write a tiny wrapper:

```javascript
function loadImageCallback(map, url, cb) {
  map.loadImage(url)
    .then(({ data }) => cb(null, data))
    .catch(cb);
}

// usage
loadImageCallback(map, url, (err, img) => {
  if (err) throw err;
  map.addImage('pin', img);
});
```

> **Tip:** Once you have the wrapper you can keep the rest of your old code unchanged, but it’s better to migrate to the promise style so you can use `await` and avoid “callback-not-called” warnings.

---

## Why the marker icons disappeared

* The image never got added → the style’s sprite has no entry called `'pin'`.  
* Any layer that references `'pin'` (`'icon-image': 'pin'`) therefore falls back to the default marker (or shows nothing if the layer is `symbol`-only).

After fixing `loadImage`, the `addImage` call will succeed and the symbols will render.

---

## Quick checklist after fixing `loadImage`

1. **Map is loaded** – `map.on('load', …)` or `map.once('load', …)` before calling `loadImage`.  
2. **Image URL is reachable** – no CORS issues; the server must send `Access-Control-Allow-Origin:*` (or your domain).  
3. **`addImage` is called only once per name** – if you call it again with the same name you’ll get `Error: Image with id "pin" already exists`. Use `map.hasImage('pin')` to guard against duplicates.  
4. **Layer uses the correct `icon-image` name** – double-check spelling (`'pin'` vs `'pin-2'`).  
5. **If you use a style that already defines a sprite**, adding images at runtime works fine; they are stored in the map’s internal sprite cache.

---

## Full minimal example (ES-module build)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – custom marker</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12
  });

  map.once('load', async () => {
    try {
      const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(
        'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/marker.png'
      );
      map.addImage('pin', img);

      // Example GeoJSON source
      map.addSource('points', {
        type: 'geojson',
        data: {
          type: 'FeatureCollection',
          features: [
            {
              type: 'Feature',
              geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] },
              properties: {}
            }
          ]
        }
      });

      map.addLayer({
        id: 'points-layer',
        type: 'symbol',
        source: 'points',
        layout: {
          'icon-image': 'pin',
          'icon-size': 0.7
        }
      });
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('❌ loadImage failed', e);
    }
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Run this in a browser; you should see a custom pin instead of the default marker.

