## TL;DR

* `map.loadImage` now returns a **Promise** – use `await` or `.then` and grab `data` from the resolved object.  
* Add the image **before** you add any layer that references it.  
* Ensure the style you’re using does **not** reference Mapbox sprite/glyph URLs.  
* Update any CSS class prefixes (`mapboxgl-` → `maplibregl-`).  

Once you make those changes, your custom marker icons will appear again and the “callback not being called” warning will disappear. Happy mapping! 🚀

### What’s happening

1. **`map.loadImage` no longer accepts a callback** –  
   Starting with **MapLibre GL v4.0.0** the method was changed to **return a `Promise`** instead of taking a `(err, image)` callback. Because the callback is ignored, the image never gets added, so any symbols that rely on `map.addImage('pin', …)` disappear from the map.

2. **Marker icons are missing** –  
   The missing icons are a direct consequence of the failed `loadImage` call. (If you were also using a style sprite, make sure the sprite URL is not a `mapbox://` URL; otherwise the same “blank-icon” symptom appears.)

---

## Fix #1 – Use the promise-based API

```javascript
// Old Mapbox-style code (does nothing in MapLibre ≥ v4)
map.loadImage(url, (err, img) => {
  if (err) throw err;
  map.addImage('pin', img);
});
```

### Option A – `async/await`

```javascript
async function addPinImage(url) {
  try {
    const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(url);   // ← returns a Promise
    map.addImage('pin', img);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to load pin image:', err);
    // handle the error (fallback image, etc.)
  }
}

// Call it after the style is ready
map.on('style.load', () => addPinImage('https://example.com/pin.png'));
```

### Option B – `.then()/.catch()`

```javascript
map.on('style.load', () => {
  map.loadImage('https://example.com/pin.png')
    .then(({ data: img }) => map.addImage('pin', img))
    .catch(err => console.error('loadImage error:', err));
});
```

> **Why wait for `style.load`?**  
> `map.addImage` can only be called **after the style (and its sprite) has been loaded**. If you call it earlier you’ll get the same “callback not called” warning because the internal worker isn’t ready yet.

---

## Fix #2 – Verify the image URL and CORS

* The URL must be reachable from the browser and must allow **CORS** (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin:*` or your domain).  
* If you’re loading a local file (`/assets/pin.png`) make sure it’s served with the correct MIME type (`image/png`).

If the request fails, the promise will reject and you’ll see the error in the console (the `catch` block above).

---

## Fix #3 – Check your style’s sprite (optional but common)

If you were relying on the default Mapbox sprite (e.g. `mapbox://sprites/...`) the style will still try to fetch that sprite and you’ll get a 401/404, which also results in missing icons. After swapping to MapLibre you need a **non-Mapbox sprite** (or no sprite at all if you add all images manually).

```javascript
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // <-- a style that uses its own sprite
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});
```

If you keep a custom style JSON, open it and replace any `sprite: "mapbox://sprites/…"` entry with a URL that points to a sprite you host (e.g. `sprite: "https://my.cdn.com/sprites/sprite"`). The same applies to `glyphs` URLs.

---

## Full minimal example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre – custom pin image</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty',
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12
  });

  // Wait until the style (and its sprite) is ready
  map.on('style.load', async () => {
    try {
      const { data: img } = await map.loadImage(
        'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js/main/docs/assets/marker.png'
      );
      map.addImage('pin', img);

      // Add a layer that uses the image
      map.addLayer({
        id: 'my-pin',
        type: 'symbol',
        source: {
          type: 'geojson',
          data: {
            type: 'FeatureCollection',
            features: [{
              type: 'Feature',
              geometry: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [-122.42, 37.78] }
            }]
          }
        },
        layout: {
          'icon-image': 'pin',
          'icon-size': 1
        }
      });
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('Could not load pin image', e);
    }
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

